            <p>
              Traditional cloud-hosted request catchers (such as legacy
              RequestBin or Webhook.site) log sensitive webhook
              payloads—including customer PII, Stripe bearer tokens,
              Authorization headers, and payment metadata—onto central server
              hard drives and database clusters. This architecture creates
              significant enterprise data compliance risks (GDPR, SOC2, HIPAA,
              PCI-DSS).
            </p>
